          "explanationKey": "Name one war fought by the United States in the 1900s.",
          "facts": [
            "The United States fought several wars in the 1900s: World War I, World War II, the Korean War, the Vietnam War and the Persian Gulf War.",
            "The United States entered World War I in 1917 because Germany attacked U.S. ships. It joined the Allied Powers: England, France, Italy and Russia.",
            "Under the Constitution, Congress has the power to declare war."
          ],
          "newWords": [
