          "explanationKey": "What was the Great Depression?",
          "facts": [
            "The Great Depression was the longest economic recession in modern history.",
            "It started with the stock market crash of 1929, called the Great Crash.",
            "Many banks closed and millions of workers lost their jobs."
          ],
          "newWords": [
            {
              "word": "depression",
              "meaning": "a long time when the economy is very weak"
